          ":question/id": "56624c75-a028-5dc9-962f-9700b721674f",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-72785",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & \u2194{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the second and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 0+(-1)(0) & 3+(-1)(2) \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
