          ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $B?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -4+(-3)(-1) & 4+(-3)(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
